151				position: absolute;
152				left: 0;
153				top: 0;
154				transform: translateY(-100%);
155				background: var(--accent);
156				color: var(--background);
157				padding: 0.75rem 1.5rem;
158				z-index: 1000;
159				border-radius: 0 0 0.25rem 0;
160				font-weight: 600;
161				text-decoration: none;
162				display: inline-block;
163			}
164			.skip-link:focus {
165				transform: none;
166				outline: 3px solid var(--text);
167				outline-offset: -3px;
168			}
169			header {
170				padding-block: 1.5rem 0;
171			}
172			header nav ul {
173				display: flex;
174				flex-wrap: wrap;
175				gap: 0.5rem 1.5rem;
176				margin: 1rem 0 0 0;
177				padding: 0;
178				list-style: none;
179			}
180			header nav li {
181				margin: 0;
182			}
183			main {
184				padding: 1rem 0;
185			}
186			main:focus {
187				outline: none;
188			}
189			section {
190				margin: 2rem 0;
191				scroll-margin-top: 1.5rem;
192			}
193			@media (forced-colors: active) {
194				.skip-link,
195				button,
196				.button {
197					border: 2px solid ButtonText;
198				}
199			}
200			.card {
201				border: 1px solid var(--border);
202				border-radius: 0.5rem;
203				padding: 1.5rem;
204				background: var(--surface);
205				margin: 1.5rem 0;
206			}
207			.card h3 {
208				font-size: 1.25rem;
209				line-height: 1.3;
210				text-wrap: balance;
211				margin-top: 0;
212				margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
213				color: var(--accent);
214			}
215			.visually-hidden {
216				position: absolute;
217				width: 1px;
218				height: 1px;
219				margin: -1px;
220				padding: 0;
221				overflow: hidden;
222				clip: rect(0, 0, 0, 0);
223				white-space: nowrap;
224				border: 0;
225			}
226			@media (prefers-contrast: more) {
227				:root {
228					--border: currentColor;
229				}
230				button,
231				.button {
232					border-width: 3px;
233				}
234				.card {
235					border-width: 2px;
236				}
237			}
238			footer {
239				padding-block: 1.5rem;
240				border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
241				font-size: 0.875rem;
242				color: var(--text-secondary);
243				text-align: center;
244			}
245			footer p {
246				margin: 0.5rem 0;
247			}
248			small {
249				display: block;
250			}
251			input,
252			textarea {
253				color: var(--text);
254				background: var(--surface);
255				border: 1px solid var(--border);
256			}
257			input:focus,
258			textarea:focus {
259				outline: 2px solid var(--accent);
260				outline-offset: 2px;
261				border-color: var(--accent);
262			}
263			@media print {
264				:root {
265					color-scheme: light;
266					--text: #000;
267					--text-secondary: #333;
268					--background: #fff;
269					--surface: #fff;
270					--accent: #000;
271					--border: #999;
272				}
273				.skip-link,
274				button,
275				.button {
276					display: none;
277				}
278				body {
279					display: block;
280					min-height: 0;
281					max-width: none;
282					padding: 0;
283				}
284				a {
285					color: inherit;
286					text-decoration: underline;
287				}
288				a[href^="http"]::after {
289					content: " (" attr(href) ")";
290					font-size: 0.85em;
291					font-weight: normal;
292				}
293				.card {
294					border: none;
295					break-inside: avoid;
296				}
297			}
298		</style>
299	</head>
300	<body>
301		<a class="skip-link" href="#main">Skip to content</a>
302		<header>
303			<h1>Welcome</h1>
304			<nav aria-label="Page sections">
305				<ul>
306					<li><a href="#features">Features</a></li>
307					<li><a href="#examples">Examples</a></li>
308					<li><a href="#resources">Resources</a></li>
309				</ul>
310			</nav>
311		</header>
312		<main id="main" tabindex="-1">
313			<section aria-label="Introduction">
314				<p>This is a well-structured, accessible HTML5 document demonstrating modern best practices for semantic markup and inclusive design.</p>
315				<p>
316					It uses semantic landmarks, a skip link for keyboard navigation,
317					and CSS that adapts to your light or dark mode preference.
318				</p>
319				<p>
320					Text and link colors meet WCAG AA contrast in both themes, type scales
321					with your browser's font size, and motion respects your system settings.
322				</p>
323			</section>
324	
325			<section aria-labelledby="features">
326				<h2 id="features">Features</h2>
327				<ul>
328					<li>Semantic HTML structure with proper landmarks</li>
329					<li>Keyboard accessible navigation and focus management</li>
330					<li>Dark mode support with custom color schemes</li>
331					<li>Responsive typography using modern CSS</li>
332					<li>Print-friendly styles for better readability</li>
333					<li>WCAG AA contrast compliance in all color modes</li>
334				</ul>
335			</section>
336	
337			<section aria-labelledby=”examples”>
338				<h2 id=”examples”>Examples</h2>
339				<article class=”card”>
340					<h3>Component Cards</h3>
341					<p>Card components are useful for organizing related content. They include a subtle border and padding for visual separation.</p>
342					<a class=”button” href=”#resources”>Learn more<span class=”visually-hidden”> about accessibility resources</span></a>
343				</article>
344	
345				<article class=”card”>
346					<h3>Interactive Elements</h3>
347					<p>Buttons and links are fully accessible with clear focus states. The “Learn more” button above demonstrates smooth transitions and proper visual feedback.</p>
348					<p>Try using the Tab key to navigate through all interactive elements.</p>
349				</article>
350	
351				<article class=”card”>
352					<h3>Accessible Form</h3>
353					<form>
354						<div style=”margin-bottom: 1rem;”>
355							<label for=”email” style=”display: block; margin-bottom: 0.5rem; font-weight: 500;”>Email <span aria-label=”required”>*</span></label>
356							<input type=”email” id=”email” name=”email” required style=”width: 100%; padding: 0.5rem; border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 0.25rem; font-family: inherit;”>
357						</div>
358						<div style=”margin-bottom: 1rem;”>
359							<label for=”message” style=”display: block; margin-bottom: 0.5rem; font-weight: 500;”>Message</label>
360							<textarea id=”message” name=”message” rows=”4” style=”width: 100%; padding: 0.5rem; border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 0.25rem; font-family: inherit; resize: vertical;”></textarea>
361						</div>
362						<button type=”submit”>Send message</button>
363					</form>
364				</article>
365	
366				<article class=”card”>
367					<h3>Live Region Example</h3>
368					<p>Click the button to announce a message using a live region. This demonstrates how screen readers are notified of dynamic updates.</p>
369					<button onclick=”announceLiveMessage()” type=”button”>Announce message</button>
370					<div aria-live=”polite” aria-atomic=”true” style=”margin-top: 1rem; padding: 1rem; background: var(--surface); border: 1px dashed var(--border); border-radius: 0.25rem; min-height: 2rem; display: flex; align-items: center;”>
371						<span id=”live-message”></span>
372					</div>
373				</article>
374			</section>
375	
376			<section aria-labelledby="resources">
377				<h2 id="resources">Resources</h2>
378				<p>Want to learn more about web accessibility and semantic HTML? Check out these resources:</p>
379				<ul>
380					<li><a href="https://www.w3.org/WAI/WCAG22/quickref/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">WCAG 2.2 Quick Reference<span class="visually-hidden"> (opens in new tab)</span></a></li>
381					<li><a href="https://html.spec.whatwg.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">HTML Living Standard<span class="visually-hidden"> (opens in new tab)</span></a></li>
382					<li><a href="https://www.a11y-101.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">A11y 101<span class="visually-hidden"> (opens in new tab)</span></a></li>
383				</ul>
384			</section>
385		</main>
386		<footer>
387			<p><small>&copy; <time datetime="2026">2026</time>. All rights reserved.</small></p>
388			<p><a href="#main">Back to top</a></p>
389		</footer>
390		<script>
391			function announceLiveMessage() {
392				const messages = [
393					"This update was announced to screen readers!",
394					"Dynamic content updates work with aria-live regions.",
395					"Live regions are essential for accessible web apps.",
396					"Try this with a screen reader like NVDA or JAWS!"
397				];
398				const randomMessage = messages[Math.floor(Math.random() * messages.length)];
399				document.getElementById('live-message').textContent = randomMessage;
400			}
401		</script>
402	</body>
403	</html>
